        "headline": "Winter Weather Advisory issued August 30 at 4:22AM AKDT until September 1 at 4:00AM AKDT by NWS Fairbanks AK",
        "description": "* WHAT...Snow and breezy winds expected. Total snow accumulations of\n5 to 8 inches across higher elevations of the Richardson Highway\nnorth of Isabel Pass, with heavier amounts above pass level. Winds\ngusting as high as 40 mph.\n\n* WHERE...Eastern Alaska Range.\n\n* WHEN...From midnight tonight to 4 AM AKDT Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be difficult. Areas of blowing snow could\nsignificantly reduce visibility.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Rain will quickly transition to snow overnight\ntonight, with",
        "severity": "Moderate",
        "certainty": "Likely",
        "urgency": "Expected",
        "sender": "NWS Fairbanks AK",
        "effective": "2026-08-30T04:22:00-08:00",
        "expires": "2026-08-30T16:00:00-08:00",
        "areas": "Eastern Alaska Range North of Trims Camp; Eastern Alaska Range South of Trims Camp",
        "category": "Met",
        "response": "Execute",
        "instruction": "Slow down and use caution while traveling. Visit 511.alaska.gov or\ncall 5 1 1 for the latest road conditions.",
